WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.128
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.428 --> 00:00:09.733
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:17.016
Unit seventeen: Essay Writing: Opinion and Discussion. Today you will plan and write a structured essay.

4
00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:19.992
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.120
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:25.926
Essay.

7
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:29.230
Essay means a piece of writing on a topic.

8
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:30.934
Write an essay.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.098
Your turn. Say: Essay.

10
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.004
Essay.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.856
Introduction.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.047
Introduction means the opening part.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.278
Begin with an introduction.

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:48.350
Your turn. Say: Introduction.

15
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.166
Introduction.

16
00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:53.744
Argument.

17
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.912
Argument means a reason for a view.

18
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:58.645
Give an argument.

19
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.670
Your turn. Say: Argument.

20
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:05.453
Argument.

21
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.125
Opinion.

22
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:10.023
Opinion means a personal view.

23
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:12.430
In my opinion, it is good.

24
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:15.274
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

25
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.042
Opinion.

26
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:20.889
Advantage.

27
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:23.697
Advantage means a good point.

28
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:25.911
One advantage is speed.

29
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:29.239
Your turn. Say: Advantage.

30
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.055
Advantage.

31
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:35.004
Disadvantage.

32
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:38.028
Disadvantage means a bad point.

33
00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:40.558
One disadvantage is cost.

34
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.953
Your turn. Say: Disadvantage.

35
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.998
Disadvantage.

36
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.925
Example.

37
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.404
Example means a case that explains.

38
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:56.109
For example, many students...

39
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:59.148
Your turn. Say: Example.

40
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.897
Example.

41
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.663
Conclusion.

42
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.487
Conclusion means the ending.

43
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.920
In conclusion, I agree.

44
00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:13.099
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

45
00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:16.830
Conclusion.

46
00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:20.959
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:23.979
Visal, how do I plan an essay?

48
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:36.481
Think of the question, write two or three main points and add an example for each. Then decide your opinion. A plan helps you write clearly and finish on time.

49
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:39.420
What structure should I use?

50
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:51.923
Use an introduction, two or three body paragraphs and a conclusion. Each paragraph begins with a topic sentence and includes a reason and an example.

51
00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:54.343
Which phrases help?

52
00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:04.360
Use In my opinion, One advantage is, However, For example and In conclusion. They show the reader how your ideas are connected.

53
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.140
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.983 --> 00:03:11.597
Grammar focus: introduction, body, conclusion.

55
00:03:11.897 --> 00:03:13.176
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:17.566
In my opinion, social media has both benefits and risks.

57
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.227
In conclusion, I believe balance is important.

58
00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:30.229
Plan first, then write an introduction, body paragraphs with examples and a conclusion. Use linking phrases to connect ideas.

59
00:03:30.983 --> 00:03:34.147
Be careful! Don't say: I write without a plan.

60
00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.413
Say: I make a plan first.

61
00:03:38.713 --> 00:03:39.946
Plan, then write.

62
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:43.200
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.384
Writing an Essay.

64
00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:48.102
Pich writes an essay about social media.

65
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.261
She plans two advantages and two disadvantages.

66
00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:55.742
Her introduction gives her opinion clearly.

67
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:59.615
Each body paragraph has a reason and an example.

68
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.901
She finishes with a short conclusion.

69
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.979
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.817 --> 00:04:11.768
An essay has an introduction, body and blank.

71
00:04:12.068 --> 00:04:15.896
A, picture. B, title only. C, conclusion.

72
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:21.421
The answer is C: conclusion.

73
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:24.351
For example gives an blank.

74
00:04:24.651 --> 00:04:28.014
A, example. B, opinion. C, ending.

75
00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.694
The answer is A: example.

76
00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.466
A plan helps you blank.

77
00:04:36.766 --> 00:04:40.582
A, stop. B, write clearly. C, write less.

78
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.284
The answer is B: write clearly.

79
00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.612
Each paragraph begins with a blank.

80
00:04:49.912 --> 00:04:53.519
A, number. B, drawing. C, topic sentence.

81
00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.519
The answer is C: topic sentence.

82
00:05:00.683 --> 00:05:01.963
What is the topic?

83
00:05:02.263 --> 00:05:06.207
A, social media. B, sports. C, music.

84
00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.265
The answer is A: social media.

85
00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:16.537
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.557
Give your opinion on social media.

87
00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.815
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:30.115 --> 00:05:41.582
In my opinion, social media has benefits and risks. It helps students share ideas, but it can waste time. Therefore, we should use it carefully.

89
00:05:41.882 --> 00:05:43.545
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:48.902
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and introduction, body, conclusion.

91
00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:53.398
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:05:53.698 --> 00:05:56.281
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:56.581 --> 00:05:58.873
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

